This is the diff of the arm that was MEASURED (`impl_bf16out.py`), which is
option C's TensorCore half only. Option C itself was not built -- see
RESULTS.md "What was not built and why". Do not mistake this one-liner for C:
on its own it moves MORE bytes than the incumbent, not fewer, and it is a
price probe, not a candidate.

`impl_bf16out.py` applies this substitution to the installed source at import
time via `_load.py`, which asserts the anchor matches exactly once, so the arm
tracks HEAD instead of a frozen copy. Line numbers below are from
streamindex_topk.py at HEAD 950974c2 (866 lines).

